  ],
  "slug": "automated-microscopy-2e31",
  "summary": "Seven items this week couple larger spatial and single-cell atlases with tools for annotating tumour cells and querying tissue microenvironments.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is consolidation of tumour and tissue transcriptomic data into queryable atlases, with spatial context increasingly built into the analysis layer. TISCH3 (477 datasets, 69 spatial collections) and CROST 2.0 (544 projects, 3538 samples, with niche, colocalization and cancer-niche tools) expand public spatial resources. PANGEA remaps 12.6M cells into a 32-type, 165-subtype hierarchy spanning 160 diseases. A pan-cancer screen across 42 cancers reports conserved tumour microenvironment programs and releases scTME. On the method side, SpaceMACE extends MACE to spatial data by combining cell-type classification, CNV inference and spatial information for tumour-cell annotation. PDAC BioPortal and the lung cancer RNA-seq study (1,824 tumors, nine clusters) show disease-specific integrations with interactive access. The items are not uniformly spatial; bulk and single-cell resources also feature.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
